    # on the number, so `\u22649 SOURCE files per increment` was compliant -- pre-existing at
    # rev67, and rev73 tripled the addresses it can drift at. Every LIVE source cap is 4;
    # `CLAUDE.md`'s 5 is the retired total and is the one declared exception, already named.
    # G4: the first cut required `\u2264`/`<=`, and `agents/software-dev.md` -- the ONE
    # address whose number matters most, since it is the agent the flow dispatches to write
    # code -- writes `Max 4 SOURCE files`. It returned `[]` there and the guard was a FLOOR
    # (`>= 6`), so the missing seventh member was invisible: `Max 9 SOURCE files` was green.
